    "description": "Petrified Wood and Agate Specimen Lot\nMineral Specimen Lot - 2 Pieces\nPolished and Natural, Brown and Tan, Vintage\nThis mineral collector's lot features two distinct geological specimens showcasing the beauty of silicified minerals. The first is a rectangular block of polished banded stone, possibly jasper or agatized petrified wood, featuring rhythmic wavy bands of sienna, tan, and cream with a translucent agate corner. The second is a natural rough specimen of petrified wood showing dark internal wood-grain patterns and a characteristic stone-hard fossilized texture.\nPolished block displays intricate wavy banding and a translucent agate section at one end\nRough specimen exhibits dark carbon-rich fossilized wood grain and bark-like outer texture\nHeavy stone-hard composition consistent with silica-replaced fossilized material\nPolished block measures approximately 7 inches in length; total lot weight 2 pounds\nCondition:\nThe polished block shows minor surface scratches and a small chip along one edge consistent with vintage display. The rough specimen remains in its natural state with jagged edges and exposed fossilized grain. No significant structural cracks observed. Finish on the block remains glossy despite light wear.\nThank you for all of your support!",
